course: dictionary
lesson: 3921
title: One word, many meanings: frost
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Frost can be a thing you see, a kind of weather, or an action. Context tells you which one. «In very hard frost road salt stops working, because even salty water freezes when it is cold enough.» Here frost means weather so cold that water freezes, and the words about freezing are the clue.
explain: Try the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «Gritters spread salt before a frost» means before very cold weather that could freeze the roads, so the meaning fits.
explain: Frost also works as a verb, to cover something with frost. In the US, to frost a cake means to put icing on it. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer chose.
fact: Frost (noun) means thin white ice crystals that form on grass, cars and windows when the air is below freezing.
fact: Frost forms on cold, clear nights, when water vapour in the air touches a very cold surface and turns straight into ice crystals.
fact: A hard frost means weather cold enough to freeze water.
fact: To frost means to cover with frost. In the US, frosting is the icing on a cake.
fact: Frosty paths and roads are slippery, and frost can damage plants, so gardeners protect them.
exercise: «The grass was white with frost this morning.» What is the frost here? | *Thin white ice crystals on the grass | Warm rain that falls in spring | A loaf of bread | A green plant that grows in shade
exercise: «In very hard frost road salt stops working.» What does hard frost mean? | Sunshine on wet roads | A hot summer wind | *Weather cold enough to freeze water | A loud noise from a car
exercise: Mia says, «I have frosted my cake with chocolate.» What did Mia do? | Burned the top of the cake | *Put icing on the cake | Ate the cake with a spoon | Froze the cake in the fridge
test: Why are frosty paths dangerous? | They are made of wood | Dry dust blows across them | They are too bright to see | *They are slippery
test: Where would frost most likely form on a clear winter night? | *A car windscreen | A cup of hot tea | A bonfire | A hot road in summer
exam: Read «Gritters spread salt before a frost because salty water freezes at a lower temperature than plain water, so ice forms less easily.» What does frost mean here? | A tasty cake topping | A broken mirror | A quiet, sleepy place | *Weather cold enough to freeze water
